From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] builder: stop trusting this fleet's riscv64 ISA extension
 probe

With the maglev Float64Min/Max fix in place, the riscv64 build_dll job
finally compiled and linked V8 end to end. build_wheel got as far as
actually running it, and died immediately:

  Fatal Python error: Illegal instruction
  ...
  File ".../py_mini_racer/_mini_racer.py", line 162 in eval
  File ".../py_mini_racer/_mini_racer.py", line 66 in __init__
  File ".../tests/test_babel.py", line 12 in test_babel

This is the first time this series has reached execution at all --
every prior riscv64 fix (gclient, CIPD, DEPS, gn args, the four GCC
compat issues, the sandbox guard, the maglev linker error) was a
compile- or link-time failure. SIGILL on a binary that just finished
compiling for the same architecture it now runs on almost always means
it contains an instruction for an ISA extension the actual CPU lacks.

V8's riscv64 CPU::CPU() (src/base/cpu.cc) asks the kernel via the
riscv_hwprobe syscall (falling back to /proc/cpuinfo's "isa" string on
pre-6.4 kernels) whether the V/Zba/Zbb/Zbs extensions are present, and
CpuFeatures::IsSupported() lets V8's RISC-V MacroAssembler emit the
corresponding instructions when it says yes -- unconditionally,
regardless of this same build's own riscv_use_rvv/riscv_use_zba/
riscv_use_zbb/riscv_use_zbs GN args, which already all default to
false (i.e. this build already targets the plain rv64gc baseline at
the source level): that runtime probe is a wholly separate mechanism,
not gated by them.

This exact fleet's riscv64 CI hardware has already demonstrated, twice
independently in this repo, that it cannot be trusted to self-report
these optional/newer extensions correctly: zlib-ng's own V-extension
runtime probe (a vsetvli instruction) SIGILLs the moment it executes,
and openvino's RVV-1.0 probe brings the whole process down instead of
safely reporting "unsupported" (see patches/zlib-ng/1.0.0/0001-*.patch
and patches/openvino/2026.4.1/0001-*.patch). A third, V8-internal
instance of the same class of bug -- some bit this probe reports set
that the real silicon does not actually implement -- is the simplest
explanation for a crash that appears only once JS actually executes.

Make V8's own riscv64 probe agree with this build's already-stated
intent: keep the FPU bit it must report for this process to have
gotten this far at all, and stop trusting it for V/Zba/Zbb/Zbs. Every
CpuFeatures::IsSupported() caller already has a correctness-preserving
fallback for when a feature is absent (the cross-compile/snapshot path
already runs with all of these off), so this only removes now-unsafe
optimized paths, it does not remove any functionality.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 CI-hardware-only ISA probe reliability issue; not a defect in V8 upstream, which has no way to know this fleet's hwprobe answers do not hold]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 builder/0002-riscv64-disable-unreliable-isa-ext-probes.patch | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 builder/v8_build.py                                          | 22 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 65 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 builder/0002-riscv64-disable-unreliable-isa-ext-probes.patch

diff --git a/builder/0002-riscv64-disable-unreliable-isa-ext-probes.patch b/builder/0002-riscv64-disable-unreliable-isa-ext-probes.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..19e7648
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builder/0002-riscv64-disable-unreliable-isa-ext-probes.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+--- src/base/cpu.cc	2026-10-16 00:00:00
++++ src/base/cpu.cc	2026-10-16 00:00:00
+@@ -1004,30 +1004,24 @@
+   riscv_hwprobe pairs[] = {{RISCV_HWPROBE_KEY_IMA_EXT_0, 0}};
+   if (!syscall(__NR_riscv_hwprobe, &pairs,
+                sizeof(pairs) / sizeof(riscv_hwprobe), 0, nullptr, 0)) {
+-    if (pairs[0].value & RISCV_HWPROBE_IMA_V) {
+-      has_rvv_ = true;
+-    }
++    // Deliberately do not trust RISCV_HWPROBE_IMA_V/EXT_ZBA/EXT_ZBB/EXT_ZBS:
++    // on this fleet's riscv64 CI hardware, the kernel's hwprobe answer (and
++    // the /proc/cpuinfo "isa" string it falls back from below) has already
++    // been observed reporting optional RISC-V extensions as present when
++    // the real silicon does not implement them, which SIGILLs the first
++    // caller that acts on it -- see the zlib-ng and openvino riscv64
++    // patches in this repo, both hitting that same class of bug for the V
++    // extension. Only trust the one bit that must be set for this process
++    // to have gotten this far at all.
+     if (pairs[0].value & RISCV_HWPROBE_IMA_FD) {
+       has_fpu_ = true;
+     }
+-    if (pairs[0].value & RISCV_HWPROBE_EXT_ZBA) {
+-      has_zba_ = true;
+-    }
+-    if (pairs[0].value & RISCV_HWPROBE_EXT_ZBB) {
+-      has_zbb_ = true;
+-    }
+-    if (pairs[0].value & RISCV_HWPROBE_EXT_ZBS) {
+-      has_zbs_ = true;
+-    }
+   }
+ #else
+   char* features = cpu_info.ExtractField("isa");
+ 
+   if (HasListItem(features, "rv64imafdc")) {
+     has_fpu_ = true;
+   }
+-  if (HasListItem(features, "rv64imafdcv")) {
+-    has_fpu_ = true;
+-    has_rvv_ = true;
+-  }
++  // See the comment above: do not trust the isa string's "v" suffix either.
+ #endif
diff --git a/builder/v8_build.py b/builder/v8_build.py
index 498516c..58b0c66 100644
--- a/builder/v8_build.py
+++ b/builder/v8_build.py
@@ -433,6 +433,28 @@ def build_v8(args: Args) -> None:
         #   V8's main branch now does.
         apply_patch("0001-riscv64-gcc-compat.patch")
 
+        # The riscv64 build/test cycle got past every GCC-compat and linker
+        # issue above and now runs V8, which promptly dies with SIGILL
+        # inside tests that just construct a MiniRacer() and eval() a
+        # trivial script: src/base/cpu.cc's riscv64 CPU::CPU() probes the
+        # kernel (riscv_hwprobe, falling back to /proc/cpuinfo's "isa"
+        # string) for the V/Zba/Zbb/Zbs extensions and, if it reports any of
+        # them present, CpuFeatures::IsSupported() lets V8's RISC-V
+        # MacroAssembler emit the corresponding instructions -- unconditionally,
+        # regardless of this same build's own use_rvv/use_zba/use_zbb/use_zbs
+        # GN args (all false; see run_build() above), since that probe isn't
+        # gated by them. This repo has already hit the same class of bug
+        # twice on this fleet's riscv64 CI hardware for the V extension
+        # alone (the zlib-ng and openvino riscv64 patches), so a third,
+        # V8-internal instance of a probed extension not actually being
+        # safe to use here is the most likely explanation for a SIGILL that
+        # only appears once real JS executes (as opposed to at compile or
+        # link time, where every prior riscv64 fix in this series showed up
+        # instead). Stop trusting that probe for the optional extensions;
+        # only the FPU bit it must report once this process has gotten this
+        # far at all is kept.
+        apply_patch("0002-riscv64-disable-unreliable-isa-ext-probes.patch")
+
     build_dir = get_v8_path() / "out.gn" / "build"
 
     run_build(build_dir, args)
--
2.43.0

